A minor correction: rn2(x) returns a number between 0 and x-1
inclusive.  Thus, the largest value i can have is 58+3*d, where d is
the level difficulty.  For this to exceed 100, d must be greater than
14.  (58+3*14 equals exactly 100.)

Also, level_difficulty() does _not_ depend on your XL in the main
dungeon: it's simply the depth of the level, with some special cases
for the endgame.[1]

Thus, dragons can only appear in throne rooms starting at DL 15, where
they make up about 3% of the monsters there.  At DL 28 -- the lowest
level where throne rooms can appear, IIUC -- about 30% of throne room
monsters will be dragons.  The increase is slightly non-linear, but
not very much so: at DL 21 the frequency of dragons in throne rooms is
a little over 17%.  (Compare to the expected 15% if it were linear.)

The Castle throne does not count as a normal throne room, and will not
have dragons, other than the four that are always generated there.


[1] If you managed to dive past a dungeon level with a throne room on
your way down and only first entered it after retrieving the amulet,
then, if I read the source correctly, level_difficulty() would return
the depth of the Sanctum instead of the current dungeon level, causing
the throne room to be populated with a very high fraction of dragons.
I doubt this happens very often, at least outside wizmode.

